# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, secret, or enormous.
#
# Without this file the build context is ~800 MB (node_modules alone is 360 MB)
# and — much worse — `.env` and `rag.db` would be uploaded to the Docker daemon
# and land in a layer. On a public Space that is the whole game.

# ── Never, under any circumstances ────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/

# Reference projects: a checked-in virtualenv and, until rotated, live
# credentials. Same reasoning as .gitignore.
related/

# Private notes and the home-infrastructure plans.
docs/jelena/
docs/ops/

# ── Rebuilt inside the image ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both forms on purpose. Docker excludes a matched directory's contents, so the
# first line is enough for it — the second removes any doubt, and makes the rule
# survive a tool that matches files rather than directories.
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
web/.next
web/out
.venv
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ── Not needed at runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.claude
.CLAUDE.md
tests/
other_agent.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
docs/

# `docs/` is excluded from the *image* only — it is not needed to run the app
# and would invalidate the layer cache on every documentation edit. It is still
# published to the Space by the deploy workflow, which copies the repo rather
# than the image. Two different things, easy to confuse.

# ── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
